 ### Resource Management with Zero Configuration Networking
-A resource management system that uses ZCN to dynamically discover and allocate HPC nodes for rendering tasks without manual configuration or downtime [S1, unofficial]. It integrates into the Virvo DVR library via the `voxserver` tool, acting as a gateway for cluster resources [S1, unofficial]. Nodes register with the resource manager at any time using ZCN. The resource manager maintains available nodes in a queue. When a user issues a rendering request, the manager waits until enough resources are available. The manager pairs the request and resource to form a rendering job, assigned to the allocated resource. The resource creates a network connection to the remote client. Rendering events are negotiated via the network I/O subsystem [S1, unofficial]. The discovery protocol uses Bonjour on Windows/macOS and Avahi on Linux [S1, unofficial].
